      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When cutting an onion, the enzyme alliinase is released, breaking down the sulfur-containing compound alliin into syn-propanethial-S-oxide and glutathione. This reaction occurs in the cell walls of the onion, releasing the gas syn-propanethial-S-oxide, which then reacts with the water in your eyes to form sulfuric acid. The sulfuric acid irritates the eyes, causing the stinging sensation, and the gas can also be absorbed through the tear ducts into the bloodstream, contributing to eye irritation.",
